# Session: 2026-07-24

**Started:** ~19:40 Dubai
**Last Updated:** ~22:23 Dubai
**Project:** SandyStudio webapp (worktree `ui-cleanup-header-modes-2ee585`)
**Topic:** UI/UX cleanup — episode header consolidation into a contextual top bar

---

## What We Are Building

A multi-step declutter of the episode page (`/episodes/[id]`) and the global
StudioShell top bar. The Director's end-vision: the non-scrolling top bar becomes
a **contextual page header** (shows the current page's identity + actions), NOT
global chrome. On the episode page it will host: episode code · title (no quotes) ·
budget · the `…` kebab. Dead/duplicate chrome is removed; scattered action buttons
collapse into the kebab; episode-level settings (governance MODE) move to Episode
Settings.

Work is split into steps, each committed + verified separately:
- **Step 1** (done): remove mockup search, ANALYTICS system-mode chip, `←Episodes`
  back-link, `BRIEF APPROVED` status chip, passive `Mode N` text. Archived episodes
  marked by sand title colour instead of a chip.
- **Step 2a** (done): collapse Refresh/Re-trigger/Mark Complete/Move-to-Trash into
  the previously-empty `…` kebab (reused existing `DropdownMenu` primitive).
- **Chunk 2b** (done): declutter the Timeline section header; move Visual check +
  STOP/Restart servers into the kebab.
- **Chunk 2c** (NOT STARTED): the big one — move episode code/title(no quotes)/
  budget/kebab UP into the sticky top bar via a portal-slot; move the MODE
  (governance) chip OUT of the top bar INTO Episode Settings.

