  with Refresh/Re-trigger/Mark Complete/Move-to-Trash. Committed `586069ee`.
- **Chunk 2b** — confirmed by: `tsc --noEmit` EXIT 0; LIVE smoke — timeline header
  reduced to `Collapse` + `Timeline` next to `All/Review/Approved/Missing` chips
  (verified via page text); kebab now also has Visual check / STOP servers (red) /
  Restart servers (verified via screenshot of open menu). Committed `d1ca8cea`.
- **Orphan removal** — `StitchStatusPill.tsx` deleted (grep confirmed zero importers
  after 2b). Committed `87f05587`.
- **Dev server runs this branch** — `preview_start name:"next-dev"` → autoPort picked
  **45597** (3000 busy = Director's prod). Compiles `/episodes` + `/episodes/[id]`
  with no runtime errors; Director's browser session already authenticated in the tab.

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Full `npm install` in the worktree** — failed: ERESOLVE, `@react-three/drei@9`
  peer conflict with `@react-three/fiber@9` (react 19). Fix: `npm install
  --legacy-peer-deps` (how the main repo is installed; no `.npmrc`).
- **`npx tsc`** — installed a bogus `tsc@2.0.4` package. Use the LOCAL binary:
  `cd webapp && npm run typecheck` (or `node_modules/.bin/tsc`).
- **Direct `eslint`** — ESLint 9 wants flat config; project lints via `next lint`.
  Use `npm run lint`.
- **Live screenshot from a fresh unauth server** — middleware redirects to `/login`;
  cannot (and must not) enter creds. Resolved because the Director's preview tab was
  already authenticated (session cookie present).

---

## What Has NOT Been Tried Yet

- **Chunk 2c portal-slot** — the mechanism to render episode header content INTO the
  sticky `StudioTopbar` from the episode page. Two options: (a) a portal into a
  known slot `<div>` id rendered by StudioTopbar (minimal, needs a mounted guard);
  (b) a small React context/provider carrying a ReactNode up to the topbar (more
  robust, one new provider). Codebase already uses `createPortal` (DropdownMenu,
  PreviewDrawer) so a portal-slot is idiomatic.
- **MODE → Episode Settings** — drop `<GovernanceChip current={episode.governance_mode} />`
  into `EpisodeSettingsCard` (it self-reads episodeId from the URL, so it works there
  unchanged); remove GovernanceChip from StudioTopbar.
- **Verify "Open final cut" still reachable** — the removed StitchStatusPill was the
  only click-to-open-final-cut affordance in the timeline header. Director said "the
  pipeline has the signal"; VERIFY the Editor/Online-Editor pipeline stage opens the
  final cut. If not, add "Open final cut" to the kebab.

